# Lab 7 – Model Evaluation Techniques

## Objective

The objective of this lab was to learn how to evaluate machine learning models beyond simple accuracy by using a confusion matrix, precision, recall, F1-score, and cross-validation.

## What I Did

In this lab, I trained and evaluated a classification model using the Titanic dataset. I generated and interpreted a confusion matrix to better understand the model's predictions, created a classification report to examine precision, recall, and F1-score, and performed 5-fold cross-validation to obtain a more reliable estimate of the model's performance. I also completed knowledge check questions that applied these evaluation metrics to real-world scenarios.

## What I Learned

This lab showed me that accuracy alone does not always provide a complete picture of a model's performance. I learned how the confusion matrix helps identify different types of prediction errors, when precision or recall should be prioritized depending on the problem, and why cross-validation produces a more dependable performance estimate by evaluating the model across multiple data splits.

## Skills & Tools

* Python
* Jupyter Notebook
* Scikit-learn
* Confusion Matrix
* Precision
* Recall
* F1-Score
* Classification Report
* Cross-Validation
* Model Evaluation

